"819","Al-Silsila-tu-Ahadees-e-Sahiha Hadees: 819 Arabic Hadees: 1712"
"820","On the authority of Umm ʿAbdullāh, the sister of Shaddād ibn Aws, who said: She sent to the Prophet ﷺ a cup of milk at the time of his breaking fast, and that was during a long day and intense heat. He sent back his messenger to her, saying: ""How did you come by this milk?"" She said: ""Milk from a sheep of mine."" He sent back his messenger to her: ""How did you come by this sheep?"" She said: ""I bought it with my own money."" So he drank it. When the next day came, Umm ʿAbdullāh came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and said: ""O Messenger of Allah, I sent you that milk out of compassion for you, because of the length of the day and the severity of the heat, yet you sent back your messenger concerning it?"" The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: ""The messengers before me were commanded not to eat except what is pure (ṭayyib), and not to act except righteously."""
"821","Al-Silsila-tu-Ahadees-e-Sahiha Hadees: 821 Arabic Hadees: 842"
