"826","Aisha said: Umm Sunbula brought milk as a gift to the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him). She came to me with it but did not find him. I said to her: ""The Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) has forbidden us from eating the food of the Bedouins."" Then the Prophet (peace be upon him) and Abu Bakr entered. The Prophet (peace be upon him) said: ""O Umm Sunbula! What is this with you?"" She said: ""Milk, O Messenger of Allah, I brought it as a gift for you."" He said: ""Pour it, O Umm Sunbula, and give it to Abu Bakr."" Then he said: ""Pour it, O Umm Sunbula, and give it to Aisha."" Then he said: ""Pour it, O Umm Sunbula."" So she gave it to the Prophet (peace be upon him) and he drank. She said: I said: ""How cool it is on the liver, O Messenger of Allah! You had forbidden the food of the Bedouins."" He said: ""O Aisha! They are not Bedouins; they are the people of our desert, and we are the people of their settlement. And when they are called, they respond. So they are not Bedouins."""
"827","Al-Silsila-tu-Ahadees-e-Sahiha Hadees: 827 Arabic Hadees: 3570"
