"834","Al-Silsila-tu-Ahadees-e-Sahiha Hadees: 834 Arabic Hadees: 2595"
"835","The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: ""It is blessed; it is food that nourishes.""Abu Dharr reported: We departed from our people, Ghifar, and they used to consider the sacred month permissible. So I set out with my brother Unays and our mother, and we alighted with an uncle of ours. Our uncle honored us and treated us well, but his people envied us. They said: ""When you left your family, Unays turned against them."" So our uncle came to us and conveyed to us what had been said to him. I said: ""As for the kindness you showed us previously, you have spoiled it, and you have no claim over us after this."" So we prepared our provisions, loaded them onto our camels, and our uncle covered himself with his garment and wept. We departed until we alighted near Mecca.Unays gambled away our provisions and their like. They went to a soothsayer who ruled in favor of Unays, and Unays returned to us with our provisions and their like with them.He said: ""I had prayed, O son of my brother, for three years before I met the Messenger of Allah ﷺ."" I said: ""For whom?"" He said: ""For Allah."" I said: ""Which direction did you face?"" He said: ""I face wherever my Lord directs me. I pray the evening prayer until the last part of the night, then I fall down as if I were a cloak until the sun rises over me.""Unays said: ""I have a need in Mecca, so suffice me."" Unays went until he came to Mecca, then returned to me. I said: ""What did you do?"" He said: ""I met a man in Mecca upon your religion who claims that Allah has sent him."" I said: ""What do the people say?"" He said: ""They say: A poet, a soothsayer, a sorcerer."" And Unays was one of the poets. Unays said: ""I have heard the speech of soothsayers, and this is not like their speech. I have compared his words to the meters of poetry, and it does not conform to the tongue of any poet after me. By Allah, he is truthful, and they are liars.""I said: ""Suffice me until I go and see."" So I came to Mecca and feigned weakness before a man from them. I said: ""Where is this man whom you call the Sabi?"" He pointed to me and said: ""The Sabi!"" So the people of the valley pelted me with every stone and bone until I fell unconscious. I rose when I rose as if I were a red idol. I came to Zamzam, washed the blood from myself, and drank from its water. I remained, O son of my brother, thirty days and nights with no food except Zamzam water. I grew fat until the folds of my belly cracked, and I found no pangs of hunger in my liver.While the people of Mecca were in a moonlit, bright night, sleep overtook them. No one circumambulated the House except two women from them invoking Isaf and Na'ilah. They passed by me in their circumambulation. I said: ""Marry one of them to the other."" They did not desist from their invocation. They passed by me again and I said: ""They are like a piece of wood, except that I do not use a euphemism."" They departed wailing and saying: ""Would that there were someone from our clansmen here!""The Messenger of Allah ﷺ and Abu Bakr met them, descending. He said: ""What is the matter with you two?"" They said: ""The Sabi is between the Ka'bah and its coverings."" He said: ""What did he say to you?"" They said: ""He said a word to us that fills the mouth.""The Messenger of Allah ﷺ came until he touched the Stone and circumambulated the House, he and his companion. Then he prayed. When he finished his prayer, Abu Dharr said: I was the first to greet him with the greeting of Islam. I said: ""Peace be upon you, O Messenger of Allah."" He said: ""And upon you be the mercy of Allah."" Then he said: ""Who are you?"" I said: ""From Ghifar."" He gestured with his hand and placed his finger on his forehead. I said to myself: ""He dislikes that I belong to Ghifar."" I went to take his hand, but his companion restrained me—he knew him better than I. Then he raised his head and said: ""How long have you been here?"" I said: ""I have been here for thirty days and nights."" He said: ""Who has been feeding you?"" I said: ""I have had no food except Zamzam water. I grew fat until the folds of my belly cracked, and I find no pangs of hunger in my liver."" He said: ""It is blessed; it is food that nourishes.""Abu Bakr said: ""O Messenger of Allah, permit me to feed him tonight."" The Messenger of Allah ﷺ and Abu Bakr went, and I went with them. Abu Bakr opened a door and began handing us raisins from Ta'if. That was the first food I ate there.Then I stayed for a while, then came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. He said: ""A land of palm trees has been shown to me, and I see it only as Yathrib. Will you convey my message to your people? Perhaps Allah will benefit them through you and reward you among them.""I came to Unays and he said: ""What did you do?"" I said: ""I have submitted and believed."" He said: ""I have no aversion to your religion, for I have submitted and believed."" We came to our mother and she said: ""I have no aversion to your religion, for I have submitted and believed.""We departed until we came to our people, Ghifar. Half of them embraced Islam, led by Aymah ibn Rahadah al-Ghifari, their chief. The other half said: ""When the Messenger of Allah ﷺ arrives in Medina, we will embrace Islam."" The Messenger of Allah ﷺ arrived in Medina, and the remaining half embraced Islam.Aslam came and said: ""O Messenger of Allah, they are our brothers; we embrace Islam upon what they embraced Islam upon."" So they embraced Islam.The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: ""Ghifar—Allah has forgiven her; Aslam—Allah has granted her safety."""
