"846","Al-Silsila-tu-Ahadees-e-Sahiha Hadees: 846 Arabic Hadees: 1471"
"847","On the authority of Thābit, from Anas ibn Mālik, that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ came to Umm Ḥarām. We brought him dates and clarified butter. He said: ""Return this to its vessel and this to its waterskin, for I am fasting."" Then he stood and led us in two rakʿahs of voluntary prayer. Umm Ḥarām and Umm Sulaym stood behind us, and he positioned me on his right side, as Thābit reckons. He led us in voluntary prayer upon a mat. When he finished his prayer, Umm Sulaym said: ""I have a special request: your servant Anas—supplicate to Allah for him."" He did not leave any good of this world or the Hereafter that day except that he supplicated for me with it. Then he said: ""O Allah, increase his wealth and his children, and bless him therein."" Anas said: ""My daughter informed me that I have been granted from my own loins ninety-odd (descendants), and no man among the Anṣār woke up possessing more wealth than I."" Then Anas said: ""O Thābit! I do not own any gold or silver except my ring."""
