"853","ʿĀʾishah (may Allah be pleased with her) said: I brought the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) a khazīrah I had cooked for him. I said to Sawdah, while the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) was between me and her: ""Eat."" She refused. I said: ""By Allah, you will eat, or I will smear your face."" She refused, so I put my hand in the khazīrah and smeared her face with it. The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) laughed, then placed his thigh for her and said to Sawdah: ""Smear her face."" So she smeared my face. The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) laughed again. Then ʿUmar passed by and called out: ""O ʿAbdullāh! O ʿAbdullāh!"" The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) thought he would enter, so he said to them both: ""Get up and wash your faces""—meaning ʿĀʾishah and Sawdah. ʿĀʾishah said: ""I continued to stand in awe of ʿUmar (may Allah be pleased with him) because of the Messenger of Allah's (peace and blessings be upon him) awe of him."""
