"873","On the authority of Abdullah ibn Busr, he said: A sheep was gifted to the Prophet ﷺ, and food was scarce that day. So he said to his family: ""Cook this sheep, and look at this flour, bake it and cook it, and make tharid with it."" He said: And the Prophet ﷺ had a large bowl called al-Gharra', which four men would carry. When morning came and they prayed the Duha prayer, that bowl was brought and they gathered around it. When the people became numerous, the Messenger of Allah ﷺ sat on his knees. A Bedouin said: ""What is this sitting posture?"" The Prophet ﷺ said: ""Allah made me a generous servant and did not make me a tyrannical, stubborn one."" Then the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: ""Eat from its sides, and leave its top, it will be blessed for you in it."" Then he said: ""Take and eat, for by the One in Whose hand is the soul of Muhammad, Allah will surely open up to you the lands of Persia and Rome, until food becomes abundant so that the name of Allah is not mentioned."""
