"888","On the authority of Ibn Abbas, he said: I entered upon my aunt Maymunah, and Khalid ibn al-Walid was with her. Maymunah said: ""O Messenger of Allah! Will you not eat from what my brother gifted me from the desert?"" So she brought two roasted lizards on a platter. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: ""Eat, for it is not from the food of my people; I find myself averse to it."" And Ibn Abbas and Khalid ate from it. Maymunah said: ""I will not eat from food that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ did not eat from."" Then the Messenger of Allah ﷺ asked for a drink, and a vessel of milk was brought. He drank, and on his right was Ibn Abbas and on his left was Khalid ibn al-Walid. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to Ibn Abbas: ""Will you permit me to give Khalid to drink?"" Ibn Abbas said: ""I would not love to give anyone preference over myself with the leftover of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ."" So Ibn Abbas took it and drank, and Khalid drank. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: ""Whoever Allah feeds with food, let him say: O Allah, bless us in it and provide us with better than it. And whoever Allah gives milk to drink, let him say: O Allah, bless us in it and increase us from it, for I do not know of anything that suffices as both food and drink except milk."""
